    "turn_idx": 104,
    "turn_text": "Well, we there's not a lot of fat right here, right, because we're so small and because we're funded. I mean, we have You know, the rules and the regulations many times are meant for larger schools. I used to use the example. When I was in the legislature, the example that I used was the coordinating board has a space model that says you should only have X number of square feet per student, right? Well, at that time, we had a course here at Sol Ross in Fairview Technology, and many of the folks at the coordinating board, and frankly, many of my fellow legislators didn't know what Fairview Technology was. Well, that's horseshoeing. We had a degree in horseshoeing. You could actually learn to horseshoe here, right? Well, by the time you put in the horse, you'd exceeded your square footage model that the coordinating board had set for you, right? So one of the challenges is that the rules are, as you say, the word is generalized, right? We generalize what a university needs, but we apply it across the board. We apply it everywhere. And there's some places where it simply doesn't work well.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
