    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70775.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 117,
    "turn_text": "That's exactly right. And so we, are very proud of the fact that we have one of the least expensive bachelor's degree programs in Texas. If you look at the degree programs on our other three campuses, Del Rio Eagle Pass and New Valley, I think that's currently the single least expensive bachelor's degree. You can get anywhere in the state. So we're very conscious of that. I mean, clearly there are times that you have to move up because the legislature provides X percent. And, you know, I mean, the truth is that every kid deserves a quality education. So I used to think of it as a glass. you know, or a bottle. And so if you can raise 30% locally, then the legislature, you need to figure out the legislature's part has to be 70% of that bottle. If you can raise 40%, then that's great, then the legislature's portion only needs. But at the end of the day, you got to be able to fill the bottle because that bottle is the student's education. That model is a student's opportunity, that model is a student's future and you need to do everything that you can to maximize that student's",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
