    "turn_text": "I love being home. I appreciate it more now, I think, than I ever appreciated it as a kid growing up here who I think every kid wants to leave home, right? But because I've now seen other parts of the world and been in other places, I love being here. But I will also tell you that it's like having four hometowns for me because I get to spend time. You know, I was 27 when I ran for the legislature. If you had called me a kid back then, I would have been really unhappy with you. But I looked back, I was a kid, right? I didn't know anything about Del Rio Eagle Pass, Oovaleo. But having had the opportunity, I mean, my favorite elementary school in the world is an elementary school in Eagle Pass, right? Because it's P.K.I.E. Elementary. And so now I get to work with Eagle Pass on the educational side. I get to work with El Rio only. And so I feel like I now have four hometowns, right? Because I go to each of them and I know the players, I know the people, I know the faculty, I know the community's issues, I helped the big huge water fight that one time between O'Valdi and Bayer County, I can tell you all about the Devil's River, I can tell you all about all of these issues historically that probably other presidents of Soros Didn't really know.",
